&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About The Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hi, I&#39;m Oussama Salimi, the Engineering Manager at N26, and I am looking for a Backend Engineer to join the Investments team here at N26.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why is this role exciting and why should you apply?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Democratize wealth: You will build a secure, real-time trading platform powering everything from Crypto and Stocks to ETFs and Managed Funds.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;High-stakes engineering: Operate at the thrilling intersection of high-speed trading and strict financial regulation where markets move fast.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;True autonomy: You are an active partner in shaping the product, not just a ticket taker. We trust you to be the owner of the delivery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Get Stuff Done Days (GSDD): Every six weeks, take two days of dedicated innovation time to explore new tech stacks, fix nagging bugs, or prototype outside the roadmap.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In This Role, You Will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Write high-quality, performant code (primarily Kotlin) and navigate the codebase fluently.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Handle deployment, bug fixing, and incident handling with a high level of independence, taking features from concept to production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Act as a sparring partner for Product Managers during Product Discovery, ensuring technical decisions support the user experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Question the status quo by asking &quot;why are we building this?&quot; and &quot;is there a simpler way?&quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Identify knowledge gaps and technical problems, taking active ownership to address them without waiting to be told.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Share your learnings from GSDD projects with the wider team, turning individual curiosity into collective knowledge.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There will be a lot more too, this is a role that will require a lot of flexibility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you need to be successful:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Proven experience as a Software Engineer taking features from concept to production with minimal supervision.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A track record of thriving in dynamic environments where requirements evolve rapidly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A growth mindset: you treat feedback as a tool for engineering excellence and have a specific plan for your own learning.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;An &quot;evidence over opinion&quot; approach: you couple every critique of a problem with a practical proposal for its solution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong proficiency in backend development, with Kotlin being our default for new services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience working with Distributed Microservices and Event-Driven Architecture (Kafka).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Good understanding of cloud infrastructure and containerization (AWS, Kubernetes, and Docker).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with observability and monitoring tools (Datadog, ELK/OpenSearch).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Resilience and proactive communication: you know how to navigate unresponsive stakeholders and unblock yourself.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Constructive dissatisfaction: you are a &quot;System Improver&quot; who proactively fixes broken processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
