&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;4,0&quot;&gt;N26’s Corporate Governance team is looking for a &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Senior Executive Associate, Corporate Governance&lt;/span&gt; to run the senior administrative engine behind our Management Board operations. Sitting at the intersection of C-suite leadership, Finance, Legal, and Risk, you will take full ownership of our executive governance workflows and high-stakes administrative processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Based in Berlin, this is a hybrid role (minimum 8 days per month in-office).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;1,0,0&quot;&gt;Drive Board &amp;amp; Committee Operations: Organise, schedule, and prepare materials for Management Board and committee meetings, ensuring presentations are uploaded on time and meet executive standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;1,1,0&quot;&gt;Review &amp;amp; Edit Executive Submissions: Assess incoming meeting materials for clarity, formatting, and clear decision objectives before they reach leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;1,2,0&quot;&gt;Handle Documentation &amp;amp; Minutes: Take official meeting minutes, track follow-up action items, and maintain secure digital archives for governance records.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;1,3,0&quot;&gt;Manage Digital Approvals &amp;amp; Tools: Coordinate document approvals via digital signature tools and keep board portals and process management systems up to date.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;1,4,0&quot;&gt;Partner Cross-Functionally: Work closely with C-suite EAs, Legal, Compliance, Finance, and Risk teams to keep committee timelines moving smoothly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;1,5,0&quot;&gt;Support Board Onboarding &amp;amp; Audits: Facilitate documentation for onboarding new Supervisory and Management Board members, and provide quick access to records during audits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;1,6,0&quot;&gt;Maintain Process &amp;amp; Regulations: Keep committee Rules of Procedure, deputy registers, and internal governance guidelines accurate and updated.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you need to be successful:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;1,0,0&quot;&gt;5+ years of executive admin experience supporting senior leaders, C-suite executives, or board operations in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;1,1,0&quot;&gt;Exposure to finance or legal stakeholders, with comfort collaborating across corporate, compliance, and leadership teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;1,2,0&quot;&gt;Fluency in English is required; German language skills are a plus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;1,3,0&quot;&gt;High organizational speed &amp;amp; quality, with a track record of handling confidential materials, meeting deadlines, and managing complex schedules smoothly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;1,4,0&quot;&gt;Strong tech &amp;amp; project skills, including experience with digital approval tools, document management, and meeting logistics (AGM or committee experience is a plus).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;1,5,0&quot;&gt;Bonus points: A degree in Business Administration, Finance, Law, or experience working within financial services/regulated environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
